<%# The editors' two head tags (`admin/pages/show`): Back never restores a panel form
    with a stale `base_updated_at` (or a stale NO ALT chip or segment count) from
    Turbo's page cache, and a hover-prefetched tile answer older than a save is
    never used for a click. %>
<%# The tab's title names the chosen image (the panel is a URL of its own). %>
<% content_for :title, [ @selected&.title.presence, "Media", "CS Studio" ].compact.join(" · ") %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="turbo-cache-control" content="no-cache">
  <meta name="turbo-prefetch" content="false">
<% end %>
<%# The Media module (media library design spec §6; round 3 Task 8, handoff §4.6):
    the header with "Upload images", the drop zone, the toolbar (search and
    segments with counts) and the grid, with the chosen image's side panel
    (`Admin::MediaLibrary::PanelComponent`) at the right -- 340px; with nothing
    chosen the grid takes the width. Choosing a tile is a link into the `content`
    frame that keeps the search, the segment, the page and the language, so Back
    returns to the previous choice. No tree column (a library image has no tree
    position of its own, the same reason Tags/Posts render plain content frames). %>
<%# Uploading (round 3, Task 9): the wrapper carries `admin--media-drop` (a file drag
    anywhere on the screen shows the overlay below and a drop hands its files to
    `admin--media-upload`) and `admin--media-upload` itself (the queue: a progress
    tile per file at the start of the grid, one at a time, nothing reloads). The
    FileDropComponent inside is the visible zone and the labelled file input; it
    stops its own drops from reaching the document-level handler twice
    (file_drop_controller.js). The header's button opens the same input. %>
<div class="mb-4 flex flex-col gap-4"
     data-controller="admin--media-drop admin--media-upload"
     data-admin--media-upload-url-value="<%= admin_media_path(**admin_url_options) %>"
     data-action="admin--media-drop:dropped->admin--media-upload#dropped">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3">
    <h1 class="text-h1 text-ink">Media</h1>
    <%= render Admin::ButtonComponent.new(label: "Upload images", variant: :primary, type: "button", data: { action: "admin--media-upload#browse" }) %>
  </div>
  <div>
    <%= render Admin::FileDropComponent.new(name: "media-upload-input", id: "media-upload-input", multiple: true, label: "Upload images",
          hint: "PNG, JPEG, GIF or WebP, up to 10 MB",
          data: { "admin--media-upload-target": "input", action: "change->admin--media-upload#filesSelected" }) %>
    <%# What each file's tile says, for a screen reader: uploaded, or not and why. %>
    <p class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-admin--media-upload-target="status"></p>
  </div>
  <%# Centred by flex over the whole window, and never in the way of the drop
      itself (`pointer-events-none`: the drag keeps its real target). %>
  <div hidden data-admin--media-drop-target="overlay" aria-hidden="true"
       class="pointer-events-none fixed inset-0 z-30 flex items-center justify-center border-2 border-dashed border-accent bg-accent-tint">
    <p class="rounded-cs bg-surface px-6 py-4 text-h2 text-ink shadow-menu">Drop images to upload</p>
  </div>
</div>

<%= render Admin::MediaLibrary::ToolbarComponent.new(counts: @counts, filter: @search.filter, q: params[:q], selected_id: @selected&.id, url_options: admin_url_options) %>

<% page_url = ->(page) { admin_media_path(list_params(:q, :filter, :selected).merge("page" => page)) } %>
<%# DOM order is visual order at every width (grid, then panel; the panel stacks
    below the grid under 1024px): no `order-*` swap, so tab order never contradicts
    what is drawn. `admin--media-panel` moves focus into the panel when a tile was
    chosen, and back to the tile when the panel is closed. %>
<div class="grid items-start gap-6 <%= "lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_340px]" if @selected %>" data-controller="admin--media-panel">
  <div class="min-w-0">
    <% if @pagination.out_of_range? %>
      <%= render "admin/shared/out_of_range_page", url: page_url.call(1) %>
    <% else %>
      <%= render Admin::MediaLibrary::GridComponent.new(assets: @assets, url_options: admin_url_options, selected_id: @selected&.id, link_params: @link_params) %>
      <% if @pagination.total_pages > 1 %>
        <div class="mt-4 rounded-cs border border-line bg-surface">
          <%= render Admin::PaginationComponent.new(pagination: @pagination, url: page_url) %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <% if @selected %>
    <%# A plain box: the panel inside is the one landmark (a `section` named by
        the image's title, and the focus target). An `aside` around it was a
        second landmark for the same thing. %>
    <div class="min-w-0 rounded-cs border border-line bg-surface p-4 lg:sticky lg:top-[calc(var(--admin-top-offset)+1.5rem)] lg:max-h-[calc(100vh-var(--admin-top-offset)-3rem)] lg:overflow-y-auto">
      <%= render Admin::MediaLibrary::PanelComponent.new(asset: @selected, locale: admin_locale, url_options: admin_url_options, link_params: @link_params) %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
